{"id": "tea:samayasara:11", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "11", "section": null}, "original": {"text": "vavahāro 'bhūyattho bhūyattho desido du suddhaṇao / bhūyattham assido khalu sammādiṭṭhī havadi jīvo", "script": "IAST (Prakrit)", "edition": "recalled by the unit author (wording believed standard; to be checked against an edition)", "licence": "public-domain text"}, "paraphrase": "The conventional standpoint is said to be unreal (abhūtārtha); the pure standpoint is taught as the real (bhūtārtha); the soul that takes refuge in the real is of right view.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:niscaya", "trm:vyavahara-naya", "trm:bhutartha", "trm:abhutartha", "trm:samyag-darsana"], "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "teachers": ["tch:kundakunda"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:12", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "12"}, "paraphrase": "The pure standpoint, which shows the pure, is to be known by those who see the supreme state; but those who still stand in the lower state are taught by the conventional standpoint.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": "vyavahara", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "consciousness-mind"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "notes": "Adhikāra-based reading of the two standpoints by the text itself.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:14", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "14", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Who sees the self as unbound and untouched, not other, constant, undifferentiated and unconjoined — know that as the pure standpoint.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:suddhatman", "trm:niscaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "teachers": ["tch:kundakunda"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:145-146", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "145-146"}, "paraphrase": "Bad karma is 'ill-natured', and good karma, you think, is 'well-natured' — but how can what leads into saṃsāra be well-natured? A fetter of gold binds a man as much as one of iron; so good and bad deeds alike bind the soul.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:punya"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-upayogas"], "notes": "Verse numbers moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:2", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "The soul established in conduct, faith and knowledge — know that as 'own-doctrine' (sva-samaya); the soul established in the units of material karma — know that as 'other-doctrine' (para-samaya).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "substance", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:sva-samaya", "trm:samaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:sva-samaya-para-samaya", "cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:38", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "38", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "I am one, pure, made of perception and knowledge, ever formless; nothing else, not even an atom, is mine.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:suddhatman", "trm:jnayaka-bhava"], "concepts": ["cpt:bheda-vijnana", "cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "practices": ["prc:bhedavijnana"], "teachers": ["tch:kundakunda"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:6", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "The knowing state (jñāyaka-bhāva) is neither 'careless' nor 'careful' — it is not any of the stages of quality; so the pure is described; what is known is simply the knower.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:jnayaka-bhava"], "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara", "cpt:fourteen-gunasthanas"], "notes": "'Careless' and 'careful' (pramatta, apramatta) name the sixth and seventh guṇasthānas, standing for all stages.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:7", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "7"}, "paraphrase": "By the conventional standpoint it is taught that the knower has conduct, faith and knowledge; in truth there is no knowledge, no conduct, no faith (as separate from him): the knower is pure.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "substance", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:niscaya", "trm:vyavahara-naya"], "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara", "cpt:three-jewels"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:8", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "8", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "As a non-Aryan cannot be made to understand except in a non-Aryan tongue, so the ultimate cannot be taught without the conventional standpoint.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": "vyavahara", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:vyavahara-naya", "trm:niscaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "teachers": ["tch:kundakunda"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "U35 contribution to a U34-owned text (core Adhyātma teaching). Amṛtacandra's numbering. Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:samayasara:kartr-karma", "source": "src:samayasara", "location": {"ref": "kartr-karma"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on doer and deed: the soul is the doer only of its own states (bhāva); material karma is done by matter; to think 'I am the doer of the other' is ignorance. Karmic matter and the soul's impure states are mutually occasioning (nimitta) without either becoming the other.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": "niscaya", "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:niscaya-vyavahara"], "terms": ["trm:karma", "trm:nimitta-upadana"], "notes": "Chapter-level ref (the kartṛ-karma adhikāra).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
